      "writtenOn": "2025-10-01T14:13:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This isn\u0027t going to work correctly. If you have WGSL like:\n\n```\nfn a() {\n  switch(4) {\n    case 2: {\n      if (true) {\n        break;\n      }\n    }\n    default: {\n      break;\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe IR ends up with:\n\n```\n%a \u003d func():void {\n  $B1: {\n    switch 4i [c: (2i, $B2), c: (default, $B3)] {  # switch_1\n      $B2: {  # case\n        if true [t: $B4] {  # if_1\n          $B4: {  # true\n            exit_switch  # switch_1\n          }\n        }\n        exit_switch  # switch_1\n      }\n      $B3: {  # case\n        exit_switch  # switch_1\n      }\n    }\n    ret\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe `ExitSwitch` is inside the inner `if` statement. So, replacing the `ExitSwitch` with an `ExitIf` for the outer if will fail validation.",
      "revId": "bcaf53c35d067c3ee18420b95f5d9cc2ac585de3",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
